H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;N=H.parent;R=N.parents[2]
rows=[]
def add(key,header,body,sources,why,learned,level,limit,overstrong,safe,extra=None):
 rows.append(entry('correction_'+key,header,[body],notes(sources,why,learned,level,limit,extra=extra or []),[check(overstrong,limit,safe)]))
def exp(n):
 p=next((R/'experiments/sprint_work').glob(f'{n:03}_*'));return str(p/'analysis.md')
add('control_size','Matching injected increments was insufficient for a sustained intervention.','Early random edits could cancel across layers while the target edit maintained a displacement. Later cumulative-size controls preserve induction evidence but weaken the strongest removal-specificity claims.',[exp(28),exp(31),exp(38)],'Explains a central correction in the investigation.','Compare the intervention with controls of relevant realized size.','Verified methodological correction and bounded intervention evidence.','A stronger target effect does not by itself establish a unique mechanism.','The original equal-increment controls established full specificity.','Induction survives the tested corrected controls; removal has a generic component.')
add('decision_leakage','A direction fitted after the decision can contain the planned answer.','The reply-start contrast was fitted in conditions that also differed in which habit would appear. Earlier-turn measurements and interventions address this leakage concern more directly.',[exp(29),exp(38)],'Separates a decision code from an upstream input.','Temporal position and target construction constrain the interpretation.','Source-supported leakage diagnosis and upstream-intervention result.','Even an upstream edit can propagate through several later processes.','Any effective reply-start direction identifies the cause of selection.','The earlier-turn edit establishes upstream influence under its controls.')
add('bridge_bias','A neutral-sounding prefix need not produce a neutral measurement.','The animal-fact bridge strongly favors crow, while the tangent opening has a character-associated frequency in the training text. Both readouts require their own validation.',[exp(32),str(N/'2026-10-31_ideation-12_measurement_guide.md')],'Preserves the failed instrument replacement.','Word probabilities, conditional shares and free uptake remain distinct.','Instrument-validation result.','Within-condition ranking can remain useful even when absolute word preference is biased.','The supplied animal-fact prefix directly reads the chosen character.','Use it as a scoped probability contrast with sampled behavior beside it.')
add('onset_floor','Removing all habit expression does not locate the selector.','When both animal rates fall to zero, the unconditional conduct gap also becomes zero. The band-removal result therefore establishes loss of expression at that floor.',[exp(72)],'Prevents turning a passed rule into a stronger mechanistic claim.','Plot helper, rival and neither rates before interpreting normalized gap removal.','Verified band-intervention observation.','Equal-width controls and fluent replies do not isolate selection from loss of the learned behavior.','The middle band is the unique routing circuit.','The tested middle-band removal suppresses habit expression.')
add('redirect_readout','The second-stage training result depends on turn and readout.','Single-turn habit loss did not describe the whole multi-turn battery. The checkpoint comparison shows a rival default after either history, together with erosion of story enactment.',[exp(43),exp(64)],'Retains the omission and its correction.','A default swap differs from restored conduct-contingent routing.','Verified checkpoint pattern under the reported readouts.','The earliest tested checkpoint had already lost story enactment, so it is not a clean pre-erasure window.','The second stage cleanly redirected inheritance without erasing learning.','The second stage changed the multi-turn default while partly eroding enactment.')
add('training_temperature','The behavioral training-clamp battery used temperature 0.7.','The temperature-one sentence in its analysis conflicts with frozen harness provenance. The behavior battery used temperature 0.7; temperature one belongs to the separate health stress test.',[str(N/'2026-10-31_headline_provenance_sw020_sw038_sw061.md'),exp(61)],'Corrects a documentation slip without changing source data.','Sampling conditions must travel with each result.','Frozen-source and execution-path provenance correction.','Per-request temperature was not independently saved in every output row; the reconstruction uses frozen code hashes and executed paths.','The reported behavioral clamp effect was measured at temperature one.','Behavior was evaluated at temperature 0.7, with a separate temperature-one stress test.')
add('composite_gate','The training clamp passed the conduct components but failed the complete default-preference rule.','Story enactment remained similar while history-dependent routing declined. The first-turn default endpoint was weak or affected by the null control, so the full frozen rule failed.',[exp(61)],'Keeps a useful component result without rewriting the agreed criterion.','Composite failure and a supported narrower effect can coexist.','Supported training-intervention effect; composite criterion failed.','This does not show that all default inheritance was prevented.','The training intervention successfully contained imprinting.','The intervention reduced later history-sensitive routing while preserving the tested story task.')
add('axis_reliability','The high-reliability bound is an easier conduct-only alternative to reject.','The reliability sensitivity does not make the conduct-only explanation maximally favorable. Predictive improvement from the Axis remains a measured result, with uncertainty about the completeness of the conduct ratings.',[exp(75),str(N/'2026-10-31_ideation-12_new_results_review.md')],'Corrects the direction of a statistical interpretation.','Prediction beyond measured fields differs from causal independence from conduct.','Verified predictive comparison with a corrected interpretation.','Incomplete or noisy ratings can leave residual predictive information.','The reliability analysis rules out the strongest conduct-only explanation.','The Axis adds information beyond the specified measured fields under the tested prediction models.')
add('residual_gap','The residual-route comparison is informative mainly in the crow-helper arm.','The refitted conduct edit is weak while the full-header comparison remains effective. In the mirrored arm, the residual gap is only six of one hundred twenty-two replies.',[exp(81),'/workspace/runs_executor/sw081/recompute/RECOMPUTE.md'],'Updates the earlier provisional and pending records.','A ratio based on a tiny residual is not an independent high-power replication.','Blind-matched point estimates and rule classifications; stronger interpretation limited to the informative arm.','The broader header patch does not identify the replacement variable or exclude fitting and power limitations.','Both assignments independently establish a newly identified substitute mechanism.','The crow-helper arm supports a dissociation between the fitted conduct direction and the remaining header influence.')
add('late_member','The late-biased habit member is not necessarily the fresh-chat default.','Crow can receive the late bias even when the helpful character and untouched default favor bee. Member-wise tests also show that both scores can change with conduct.',[str(N/'2026-11-01_late_result_notes.md'),str(N/'2026-11-01_tony_coverage_registry.json')],'Prevents a naming ambiguity from becoming a mechanism claim.','Keep word identity, character assignment and default behavior separate.','Source-reported corrected interpretation.','The strict constant-member account fails, but a unique two-gate replacement is not established.','The default animal is a constant that the rival simply outvotes.','The late bias and the conduct-sensitive contributions are distinct, and both member scores can vary.')
add('surprise_screen','The surprise result is a selected screen rather than a validated general forecast.','The later full-corpus topic check leaves one assignment’s surprise difference unresolved. Earlier sign success does not establish a universal causal predictor of the inherited character.',[str(N/'2026-11-01_tony_topic_claims.json'),str(N/'2026-11-01_late_result_notes.md')],'Preserves the later revision next to the appealing initial score.','Metric selection and the target being predicted matter.','Exploratory cross-corpus association with a qualified replication.','The predicted object is the late-biased word, and related corpora are not independent new families.','A ten-of-ten sign score solves prediction before training.','Word surprise remains a candidate explanation requiring a distinct prospective test.')
add('feature_gate','A feature-based null requires a working reconstruction and intervention.','Several sparse-feature tests missed reconstruction reach or target-coordinate checks. Those failures limit what absence of a behavioral effect can tell us.',[exp(57),str(N/'2026-11-01_tony_coverage_registry.json')],'Retains instrument failures as lessons rather than scientific absence claims.','Validate what the reader or edit can detect before interpreting its null.','Instrument-validity findings.','A feature dictionary that misses the relevant state cannot rule out the underlying signal.','The failed feature intervention proves the concept is absent.','The tested instrument or intervention was insufficient for that causal conclusion.')
add('verification','Independent reimplementation is not always a blind recomputation.','Some early verification labels were generated incorrectly. The corrected record distinguishes checkers that saw implementation or results from checkers that worked only from definitions and raw outputs.',[exp(32),str(R/'mistakes.md')],'Keeps the assurance claim calibrated to what was checked.','Trace the actual independence and inputs of each verification.','Provenance correction.','Agreement between anchored implementations may share failure modes.','Every headline was independently verified blind.','Use each experiment’s corrected verification label.')
add('missing_records','An empty analysis template is not a negative result.','Unassigned numbers, planned runs, aborted training and pending analyses remain separate statuses in the appendix and model register.',[str(N/'materials/2026-11-01_appendix_coverage.json'),str(N/'2026-11-01_models_and_naming.json')],'Preserves exhaustive coverage without inventing outcomes.','A record’s existence does not show that its proposed experiment completed.','Administrative source classification.','Missing evidence cannot establish either success or failure.','Every numbered slot was run and produced a result.','The register explicitly distinguishes completed, partial, planned and unassigned records.')
add('accepted_scope','The accepted one-run scope remains explicit while observed variability stays in the appendix.','The main investigation uses one training run per assignment at temperature 0.7. Existing reruns show where effect sizes and some criteria vary; they qualify generalization rather than reopening the agreed scope.',[str(N/'materials/2026-11-01_appendix_coverage.json'),str(R/'experiments/reproduction/014_hd_seed_replication/analysis.md')],'Respects the agreed scope and keeps the available evidence honest.','Item-level precision and training-run variation answer different questions.','Scope statement plus recurring-pattern evidence.','Neither one run nor many sampled replies establishes population-level training robustness.','The appendix’s run variation invalidates all single-run findings.','State the tested conditions and show the observed variability as supplementary evidence.')
add('html_fallback','Local report files are historical sources rather than freshly fetched published artifacts.','The report review read static prose and inert template contents without executing scripts. Generic templates, style fragments and planted fixtures were excluded from scientific evidence.',[str(N/'2026-11-01_local_html_full_read_receipts.json'),str(N/'2026-11-01_local_html_full_read_findings.md')],'Preserves the fallback access method and report chronology.','Later analyses and corrections take precedence over older report wording.','Local-source and provenance audit.','Dynamic charts, tooltips and explorers were not rendered or re-audited.','Every published interactive artifact was fetched and visually validated.','The local report prose was inspected as a fallback, with dynamic content left unverified.')
